  "name": "two-cabs-26",
  "title": "Two cabs, 26 players",
  "description": "Two cabs, 26 players, 13 rounds played in parallel pairs with disjoint tappers. The final round is played alone on one cab. Each round's drafters and gamblers are everyone not tapping it, and nobody drafts both games of a slot. Everyone taps 5 times, drafts once and gambles 7 times.",
  "critique": "Co-occurrence is 1281, exactly the proven lower bound, so no schedule mixes players more evenly. Pairs tap together 0-3 times. 9 pairs never tap together. With more than 20 players, 6 people sit out tapping in each parallel slot and gamble on both games, so waits come back (longest: 2 slots) and late rounds are no longer shared automatically. Late-round value ranges 2.52-3.25 around a mean of 2.88 (imbalance 547).",
